## Summary

Update runner.go to use the new SignalParser for v2 pilot-signal blocks, with fallback to legacy NAVIGATOR_STATUS parsing.

## Dependencies

- Requires GH-939 (signal.go) to be merged first

## Implementation

### 1. Add SignalParser field to Runner struct (~line 130)

```go
type Runner struct {
    // ... existing fields ...
    signalParser *SignalParser
}
```

### 2. Initialize in NewRunnerWithConfig

```go
func NewRunnerWithConfig(config *ExecutorConfig) *Runner {
    r := &Runner{
        // ... existing ...
    }
    r.signalParser = NewSignalParser(r.log)
    return r
}
```

### 3. Update parseNavigatorPatterns() (lines 2694-2760)

```go
func (r *Runner) parseNavigatorPatterns(taskID, text string, state *progressState) {
    // Try v2 signals first
    if r.signalParser != nil {
        signals := r.signalParser.Parse(text)
        for _, sig := range signals {
            switch sig.Type {
            case SignalTypeStatus:
                r.handleV2StatusSignal(taskID, &sig, state)
            case SignalTypeExit:
                if sig.ExitSignal {
                    state.completed = true
                    state.progress = 100
                    r.reportProgress(taskID, "Completed", 100, "Exit signal received")
                }
            case SignalTypePhase:
                r.handleV2PhaseSignal(taskID, &sig, state)
            }
        }

        // If we found v2 signals, skip legacy parsing
        if len(signals) > 0 {
            return
        }
    }

    // Legacy parsing (backward compatibility)
    // ... existing code ...
}

func (r *Runner) handleV2StatusSignal(taskID string, sig *PilotSignal, state *progressState) {
    state.phase = sig.Phase
    state.progress = sig.Progress
    state.iteration = sig.Iteration

    phase := sig.Phase
    if phase == "" {
        phase = "Working"
    }

    r.reportProgress(taskID, phase, sig.Progress, 
        fmt.Sprintf("Iteration %d/%d", sig.Iteration, sig.MaxIter))
}

func (r *Runner) handleV2PhaseSignal(taskID string, sig *PilotSignal, state *progressState) {
    state.phase = sig.Phase

    // Map phases to progress
    phaseProgress := map[string]int{
        "RESEARCH": 25,
        "IMPL":     50,
        "VERIFY":   80,
    }

    if p, ok := phaseProgress[sig.Phase]; ok {
        state.progress = p
    }

    r.reportProgress(taskID, sig.Phase, state.progress, "Phase transition")
}
```

### 4. Add validation to legacy parser (lines 2762-2805)

In `parseNavigatorStatusBlock()`, add:

```go
// Clamp progress to valid range
if progress < 0 {
    r.log.Warn("Legacy parser: clamping negative progress",
        slog.String("task_id", taskID),
        slog.Int("original", progress),
    )
    progress = 0
}
if progress > 100 {
    r.log.Warn("Legacy parser: clamping progress > 100",
        slog.String("task_id", taskID),
        slog.Int("original", progress),
    )
    progress = 100
}
```

### 5. Update prompt (~line 2273) for v2 format

In BuildPrompt(), update the Navigator instructions:

```go
// Old:
sb.WriteString("- Output NAVIGATOR_STATUS blocks for progress tracking\n")

// New:
sb.WriteString("- Output progress in pilot-signal JSON blocks:\n")
sb.WriteString("  ```pilot-signal\n")
sb.WriteString("  {\"v\":2,\"type\":\"status\",\"phase\":\"IMPL\",\"progress\":45}\n")
sb.WriteString("  ```\n")
```

